in Corporation (NYSE: OLN) (\"Olin\") and Huntsman Corporation (NYSE: HUN) (\"Huntsman\") announced\nthat on July 13, 2026, the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission declared effective the\nregistration statement on Form S-4 (the \"Registration Statement\") filed by Olin in connection with\nthe previously announced all-stock merger of equals (the \"Transaction\") to form a combined company,\nOlinHuntsman. \n\n[Learn More][78]\n\n## Huntsman to Discuss Second Quarter 2026 Results on July 31, 2026\n\nWe will hold a conference call on Friday, July 31, 2026, at 10:00 a.m. ET to discuss our second\nquarter 2026 financial results. Following opening remarks, the call will move into a question and\nanswer session.\n\n[Learn More][79]\n\n## Our 2025 Sustainability Report is Here\n\nFrom innovation to impact- see how we’re advancing solutions that power more sustainable products.\n\n[Read now ][80]\n\n## SHOKLESS™ systems for electric vehicle (EV) batteries\n## What’s inside matters…\n\nDeveloped to encapsulate EV battery cells, our portfolio of polyurethane-based SHOKLESS™ systems are\nlightweight, shock-resistant, thermally optimized and structurally strong – supporting OEMs and\nbattery manufacturers as they work to enhance the next generation of batteries powering EVs.\n\n[Find out more][81]\n\n## Are you looking for solutions to your challenges? Explore our digital portfolio!\n\nSearch for products faster by application, chemistry, or performance attributes—with just a few\nclicks using our new product finder.\n\n[Search Products][82]\n\n## Our Technology Portal Fosters Innovation and Manufacturing Driven Collaborations\n\nAnd we want to work with you! Partner with us to scale your innovation and unlock business\nopportunities today.\n\n[Learn More][83]\n\n### Latest News\n\nJul 14, 2026\n\n[OLIN and HUNTSMAN Announce S-4 Registration Statement in Connection with Planned Merger is\nEffective][84]\n\n[View All][85]\nJun 30, 2026\n\n[Huntsman to Discuss Second Quarter 2026 Results on July 31, 2026][86]\n\n## Enriching lives through innovation\n\nFor over 50 years, and in approximately 25 countries, our 6,000 associates have been using science\nand ingenuity to create innovations that play a critical role in the everyday lives of many millions\nof people.\n\n[About Huntsman][87]\n\n## Markets\n\n### Aerospace and Defense\n\nImproving assembly productivity, reducing weight and extending the lifetime of parts are imperative\nto reduce costs in the aerospace and defense sector. As a leading global supplier of\nhigh-performance materials, Huntsman’s products help customers improve production processes, realize\ncomplex designs, reduce weight, and remain compliant with stringent standards and\nlower long-term maintenance costs.  \n\n[View Market][88] [View All Markets][89]\n\n### Automation, Robotics and Engineering\n\nOur polyurethane and thermoplastic polyurethane (TPU) elastomers and casting machines are used\nacross many industries to create components and technical parts for a range of applications. In\nmanufacturing, our materials improve the performance of parts in hydraulic, robotic and conveying\nequipment, supporting the growth of smart"
