    Governance\n    * [ Corporate governance ][74]\n    * [ Board of Directors ][75]\n    * [ Shareholders meetings ][76]\n  * [ Regulated news ][77]\n  * [ Contacts ][78]\n\n# We are essential chemistry, making progress possible for generations\n\n[Logistics and Traceability Operations at the La Rochelle Site]\n\n## Reducing emissions across our European logistics network\n\nFrom biofuels in France to electric transport in Germany, Solvay works with partners to scale\npractical solutions.\n\n[Read the article][79]\n[La Rochelle site]\n\n## Solvay and Viridis sign letter of intent (LOI)\n\nStrategic partnership aimed at securing critical feedstock to meet global rare earth demand.\n\n[Read the news][80]\n[Philippe signs contract with Pantys]\n\n## Solvay and Pantys expands its partnership\n\nThree-year collaboration applies social credits to measure and scale improvements in people’s daily\nlives.\n\n[Read the news][81]\n\n## 2025 key figures\n\n~8,400 employees\n43 production sites\n41 countries\n€4.3bn net sales\nNow at Solvay\n[Press release]\nPress releases\n\n### [Participation notification by SIH Partners - July 7, 2026][82]\n\nJul 07, 2026\n[ Opens in a new window ][83] [ Opens in a new window ][84]\n[Linne Herten Tiny Forest Planting Day - March 20, 2025Linne Herten tree planting day]\nPress releases\n\n### [Solvay channels internal travel carbon pricing into local climate and nature projects ][85]\n\nMay 22, 2026\n[ Opens in a new window ][86] [ Opens in a new window ][87]\n[AGM - Philippe Kehren]\nPress releases\n\n### [Outcome of Solvay’s 2026 shareholders’ meeting][88]\n\nMay 12, 2026\n[ Opens in a new window ][89] [ Opens in a new window ][90]\n[Worker smiling at la Rochelle]\nCreating sustainable impact\n\n## For Generations\n\n\"For Generations\" signifies our dedication to acting responsibly today to ensure a positive legacy\nfor those who come after us. Building on our process expertise and on our core beliefs, this program\nis designed to foster trust and create value for Solvay, its stakeholders, and society as a whole. \n[Learn about the program][91]\n[AIR Cover_1022x506px - 1]\n\n## Annual Integrated Report\n\nIn 2025, Solvay delivered on its commitment to excellence in both financial and sustainability\nperformance despite a macroeconomic environment marked by geopolitical and  economic uncertainties. \n\n[Read our latest Annual Report][92]\n[Solvay employees in France]\n\n## Join our team and thrive\n\nWe actively seek employees whose personal values resonate with ours, as this alignment is integral\nto fulfilling our mission. The journey begins with a steadfast commitment to our company’s core\nvalues and purpose. We are essential chemistry, making progress possible for generations.\n\n \n\n[Discover Life at Solvay][93]\n\n## We are essential chemistry, making progress possible for generations.\n\nSolvay, a pioneering chemical company with a legacy rooted in founder Ernest Solvay's pivotal\ninnovations in the soda ash process, is dedicated to delivering essential solutions globally through\nits workforce of around 9,000 employees. Since 1863, Solvay harnesses the power of chemistry to\ncreate innovative, sustainable solutions that answer the world’s most essential needs such as\npurifying the air we breathe and the water we use, preserving our food supplies, protecting our\nhealth and well-being, creating eco-friendly clothing, making the tires of our cars more sustainable\nand cleaning and protecting our homes. Solvay’s unwavering commitment drives the transition to a\ncarbon-neutral future by 2050, underscoring its dedication to sustainability and a fair and just\ntransition. As a world-leading company with €4.7 billion in underlying net sales in 2024, Solvay is\nlisted on Euronext Brussels and Paris (SOLB).\n* [e-Business][94]\n* [Contact Us][95]\n* [Suppliers][96]\n* [Ethics Helpline][97]\n* [Sitemap][98]\n* [Solvay's Privacy & Cookie Policy][99]\n* [Terms and Conditions and Legal Notice][100]\n* [D