one company: a new identity, built on continuity.\n\nOur new chapter builds on the foundations that have made us strong: deep technical expertise,\nlong-standing customer relationships, trusted heritage brands, and a culture shaped over more than\n130 years. As an independent company, we now move with greater entrepreneurial freedom, faster\ndecision-making and agility, backed by Carlyle's global network and commitment to our growth.\n\n[ Press Release ][62]\n\nI agree to the transfer of my personal data to Google in order to display contents provided by\nYouTube. I have read the [privacy policy][63].\n\nSubmit\n\n## What defines us\n\nOur intelligent coatings help customers shine in their markets. We anticipate global trends and\nidentify opportunities that shape the future of industries. We meet the highest technical and\nquality demands in an aesthetically pleasing, environmentally friendly way, combining design with\nfunctionality. Our work in research, production and service is reliable worldwide.\n\n### Driven by passion and science\n\nBuilt on BASF's heritage with a more entrepreneurial future, we foster an inspiring exchange across\ndiverse perspectives.\n\n[ Careers ][64]\n\n### Merging science and beauty\n\nClose collaboration, global presence, expertise and innovation are the pillars of our commercial\nsuccess.\n\n[ About us ][65]\n\n### Reliable worldwide\n\nAround 10,000 employees at our more than 70 sites of Surventis are ready to serve, wherever you are\nlocated.\n\n[ Locations ][66]\nImage\n[Purple automotive coating]\n\n## What we do\n\nWe engineer coatings and surface solutions, from treatment to refinish, across automotive and many\nother industries. Working with us means going further to solve even your most challenging needs.\n[\nImage\n[back 3/4 view of a white car with a sunset in the background] ][67]\n\n### Automotive\n\nOur solutions support a broad range of vehicle categories and powertrain concepts, helping\nmanufacturers, suppliers, body builders and bodyshops create the surfaces that keep the automotive\nworld moving.\n[Learn more][68]\n[\nImage\n[airplane flying view from inside window of aircraft, flying above the clouds during sunset] ][69]\n\n### Aerospace\n\nWith decades of aerospace experience and a broad portfolio of OEM approved technologies, we support\na wide range of aircraft types and applications.\n[Learn more][70]\n[\nImage\n[detail of steel coils in warehouse] ][71]\n\n### Coil\n\nWe support the coil industry with surface treatment and advanced application technologies that\nprepare and protect metal before it is shaped and coated.\n[Learn more][72]\n[\nImage\n[motorcycles parked in row in various colors] ][73]\n\n### Specialty\n\nFrom a perfectly smooth piano finish to precise optical components and durable motorcycle surfaces,\nwe help each surface perform as intended in its own context.\n[Learn more][74]\nImage\n[White]\n\n## What sets us apart\n\nFrom the world's most advanced color expertise to award-winning sustainable innovation, these are\nsome of the capabilities that make us a partner unlike any other.\n\n[\nImage\n[Refinity app on tablet] ][75]\n\n### Refinity® – a seamless digital experience for bodyshops\n\nOur cloud-based platform brings together a full suite of digital solutions for automotive refinish,\nhelping body shops worldwide work faster, more sustainably and with the most advanced digital color\nexperience available.\n[Discover Refinity®][76]\n[\nImage\n[Tesseract blue] ][77]\n\n### Automotive Color Trends – DRIVING THE PROXY\n\nEach year our designers shape the colors of tomorrow's vehicles. Our latest collection draws on\ndesign, nature and technology, with sustainable materials and innovations like multi-color pigments\nand liquid-metal surfaces.\n[Explore the collection][78]\n[\nImage\n[Automotive color display] ][79]\n\n### The world's largest color databases\n\nDecades of color expertise, captured in one of the world's largest databases. It lets us match and\nreproduce virtually any shade with precision, whether designing tomorrow's vehicles or restoring\ntoday's.\n[Our color expertise][80]\n[\nImage\n[R-M expert] ][81]\n\n### Trusted heritage brands\n\nBehind Surventis stands a portfolio of brands the industry has relied on for generations. Glasurit®,\nwith over 130 years of refinish expertise, and R-M®, with more than a century of color leadership,\nare recognized by bodyshops and manufacturers worldwide, alongside specialist brands like baslac®\nand Norbin®. These names carry a legacy of quality that continues into our new chapter.\n[Meet our brands][82]\n\n## Latest News\n\n[[Surventis Flags] ][83]\nNew\nCorporate\n\n### [ Surventis launches as an independent global leader in automotive coatings and surface\n### treatment ][84]\n\nMUENSTER, Germany, July 1, 2026. Surventis, formerly BASF Coatings, today launched as an independent\ncompany, completing its carve-out from BASF. With around €3.9 billion in annual sales and around\n10,700 employees, Surventis is one of the world’s leading suppliers of automotive coatings and\nsurface treatment solutions. The business is majority-owned by funds managed by global investment\nfirm Carlyle (NASDAQ: CG) in partnership with Qatar Investment Authority. BASF holds a 40% stake in\nSurventis.\nJul 1, 2026\n[[Image of the executive committee of Surventis] ][85]\nNew\nCorporate\n\n### [ BASF Coatings names Executive Committee to lead and drive success as a standalone company\n### ][86]\n\nMUENSTER, Germany, June 25, 2026. BASF Coatings today named the leadership team that will run the\nbusiness as an independent company from July 1, 2026, after the closing of the transaction. The new\nstructure brings together leaders who have built the coatings business over many years and senior\nexecutives with proven records in finance, digital and transformation. The Executive Committee will\nbe led by incoming Chief Executive Officer Jens Luehring.\nJun 26, 2026\n[[Group picture of recipients of the SQIP Award 2026] ][87]\nNew\nSurface Treatment\n\n### [ Chemetall receives Airbus SQIP award for the eleventh consecutive year ][88]\n\nJun 24, 2026\n[[Light Grey] ][89]\nInnovation\nOEM Coatings\nDigitalization\nSustainability\n\n### [ BASF completes the sale of its Brazilian decorative paints business to Sherwin-Williams ][90]\n\nThe sale of BASF’s Brazilian decorative paints business to Sherwin-Williams was completed on October\n1, 2025, following the approval of the transaction by the relevant Brazilian competition authority\nat the end of August 2025. On a cash and debt-free basis, the purchase price amounted to $1.15\nbillion.\nJun 9, 2026\n[ View all news ][91]\n\n## Global reach, local expertise\n\nOperating across 100 countries with more than 30 production sites close to customers – guaranteeing\nsupply security, fast lead times and on-site technical support wherever customers operate.\n\n[ Get in touch ][92]\n[ Our locations ][93]\n\nLooking for your next career move? Visit our [Careers][94] section\n\n## Footer\n* ### Industries\n  * [Aerospace][95]\n  * [Automotive][96]\n  * [Coil][97]\n  * [Specialty][98]\n* ### About\n  * [About us][99]\n  * [Locations][100]\n  * [Driving Diversity][101]\n  * [Procurement][102]\n  * [Code of Conduct][103]\n  * [Certificates][104]\n* ### Sustainability\n  * [Our commitment][105]\n* ### Media\n  * [All News][106]\n  * [Media Contacts][107]\n* ### Careers\n  * [Join us][108]\n* ### Contact\n  * [Contact us][109]\n\n[ ][110]\n* Copyright © Surventis 2026\n* Cookie Preferences\n* [Disclaimer][111]\n* [Legal Notice][112]\n* [Privacy Policy][113]\n\n[1]: #main-content\n[2]: /\n[3]: /\n[4]: /home\n[5]: /aerospace\n[6]: /automotive\n[7]: /surface-treatment\n[8]: /light-vehicles\n[9]: /heavy-duty\n[10]: /automotive-components\n[11]: /refinish\n[12]: /color\n[13]: /digital-solutions\n[14]: /processes\n[15]: /coil\n[16]: /specialty\n[17]: /piano-coatings\n[18]: /motorcycle-coatings\n[19]: /lighting-solutions\n[20]: /ab