plications\n\n#### High-tech . Ultra-light . High-strength\n* [ See Details ][68]\n\n### High Performance\n\n#### Lighter weight . Higher performance . Lower cost\n* [ See Details ][69]\n\n### Interesting News\n\n#### Innovative . Relevant . Groundbreaking\n* [ See Details ][70]\n\n### Sustainable Future\n\n#### Mega-stable . Light weight . Ultra-thin\n* [ See Details ][71]\n\n## Your partner for advanced carbon fiber solutions.\n\n[\n\n### Our Products\n\nTeijin is one of the world's leading manufacturers of high-performance carbon fiber products. Tenax™\nCarbon Fiber is the benchmark for use as filament yarns and short fibers. Learn more about Teijin's\ncarbon fiber products.\n\n][72] [\n\n### Our Markets\n\nTenax™ Carbon Fiber is a versatile, strong, durable and reliable material used in many industrial\nand consumer applications. Learn more about the industries using Teijin's carbon fiber products.\n\n][73]\n\n## About Us\n\n[\n\n\n## Fair Guide\n\n][74] [\n\n\n## Jobs & Careers\n\n][75] [\n\n\n## Processing\n\n][76]\n[\n\n## Teijin Carbon Online\n\nTeijin delivers products and services that create \"new value\" to customers.\n\n][77]\n[\n\n07. July 2026\n\n##### Defining the \"Goldilocks\" Application Zone for Thermoplastic Braid and Vacuum Bag Only\n##### Consolidation\n\n[Alfonso Lopez delivering a presentation at TCC 2026 on thermoplastic braid and vacuum bag only\nconsolidation for advanced composite manufacturing.]\n\n\nWith thermoplastic composites moving toward broader industrial adoption, manufacturers need to\ndecide which process route delivers the best balance between geometric flexibility, consolidation\nquality, infrastructure requirements and production scalability for their products. \n\n][78]\n[\n\n02. July 2026\n\n##### From Engineering Performance to Industrial Reality: Why aerospace manufacturing logic matters\n##### in high‑performance cycling\n\n[Road cyclist climbing a mountain road on a high-performance bicycle surrounded by a natural\nlandscape.]\n\n\nAs high-performance cycling structures become more integrated and complex, performance is no longer\ndefined by weight alone. Aerospace manufacturing principles such as process stability,\nreproducibility and controlled rapid-curing technologies are increasingly shaping how predictable\ncomposite performance is engineered, scaled and maintained under real-world conditions. \n\n][79]\n[\n\n21. Mai 2026\n\n##### From Lightweight to Intelligent Structures:What Sea Otter Classic 2026 reveals about the\n##### future of performance materials\n\n[Close-up action shot of a mountain bike riding over a rocky trail, with dirt and gravel spraying\nfrom the rear wheel, highlighting performance, durability, and off-road cycling conditions.]\n\n\nPerformance cycling is often seen as a playground for marginal gains. What became visible at Sea\nOtter Classic 2026, however, points to a deeper shift: The limiting factor in performance is no\nlonger weight – it is the ability to engineer predictable performance under real-world conditions. \n\n][80]\n\n[More][81]\n\n \n\n[ Close][82]\n* [Deutsch][83]\n* [Japanese][84]\n* [Chinese][85]\n[Close][86]\nSearch\n* [ Page top][87]\n* [ Search][88]\n* [Products][89]\n  [Products][90]\n  * [Filament Yarn][91]\n  * [Short Fibers][92]\n  * [ThermoPlastics][93]\n  * [ThermoSets][94]\n  * [Dry Reinforcements][95]\n  * [Pyromex][96]\n* [Markets][97]\n  [Markets][98]\n  * [Aerospace][99]\n  * [Automotive][100]\n  * [Civil Engineering][101]\n  * [Renewable Energies][102]\n  * [Industrial][103]\n  * [Marine][104]\n  * [Medical][105]\n  * [Oil and Gas][106]\n  * [Sporting Goods][107]\n* [Processing][108]\n  [Processing][109]\n  * [Prepreg][110]\n  * [Weaving][111]\n  * [Braiding][112]\n  * [Winding][113]\n  * [Pultrusion][114]\n  * [Compounding][115]\n  * [Non-Crimp Fabric][116]\n  * [SMC][117]\n* [About Us][118]\n  [About Us][119]\n  * [Global Network][120]\n  * [Certificates][121]\n  * [Fair Guide][122]\n  * [Teijin Limited][123]\n  * [