          "summary": "Nature. Future. Us.[TENCEL™ for Business][1]\n[Nature][2]\n[Future][3]\n[Us][4]\n\nMove, breathe and live in harmony with nature.\n\n[TENCEL™ Studio][5][TENCEL™ Lab][6][TENCEL™ Stories][7][Sustainability Report][8]\n[Fibers][9]\n\nWe respect both people and planet.\n\n[What is TENCEL™][10][Benefits][11][TENCEL™ in Our Lives][12]\n[TENCEL™ for Business][13][Search]\n[Nature][14]\n[Future][15]\n[Us][16]\n[TENCEL™ Studio][17][TENCEL™ Lab][18][TENCEL™ Stories][19][Sustainability Report][20]\n\nMove, breathe and live in harmony with nature.\n\n[Fibers][21]\n[What is TENCEL™][22][Benefits][23][TENCEL™ in Our Lives][24]\n\nWe respect both people and planet.\n\n[search icon]\n[close icon]\nYour browser does not support the video tag.Your browser does not support the video tag.\n\n# TENCEL™ Fibers for Fabrics and Textile\n\nRead more on [What makes us][25].\n\nOur fibers are derived from natural raw material wood, with a lower impact,[¹][26]and provide\nlong-lasting comfort.[²][27]\n\n[Explore our fibers][28]\n[TENCEL™ icon representing fibers are made with less carbon emissions and water comsumption]\n[TENCEL™ icon symbolizing wood-based origin and sourced from responsibly managed forests]\n[TENCEL™ certification icon representing certified with the EU Ecolabel]\n[TENCEL™ sustainability icon symbolizing fibers are made from certified wood sources]\n[TENCEL™ icon symbolizing fibers are certified as biodegradable and compostable]\n\nTENCEL™ Lyocell and Modal fibers are made with at least 50% less carbon emissions and water\nconsumption[^{1}][29]\n\n[Explore our fibers benefits][30]\n[Sustainable forest landscape symbolizing the renewable wood sources used in TENCEL™ fiber\nproduction]\n\n## Nature\n\nTENCEL™ weaves together the story of nature and people.\n[Explore][31]\n[An industrial robotic arm operating within Lenzing's advanced manufacturing facility, reflecting\nthe precision-driven production technologies behind TENCEL™ Lyocell and Modal fibers.]\n\n## Future\n\nWe pioneer industry leading technologies to drive innovation.\n\n[Explore][32]\n[Parent carrying child on shoulders outdoors, representing the connection between TENCEL™ and\ncollaborators and innovators]\n\n## Us\n\nFrom brand collaborators to innovators, we connect through our ability to dream.\n[Explore][33]\nOur community\nWe are\nbrands\ndesigners\ncreators\ninnovators\nscientists\nideators\ncollaborators\ntrailblazers\nnature\nfuture\nus\nyou\n[Explore our community][34]\n\n## TENCEL™ Studio\n\nCollaboration is the first step towards a more sustainable future.[¹⁰][35]\n\n[Find out more][36]\n[prev]\n[prev]\n\n### Eberjey: 30 years of comfort with TENCEL™ Modal\n\n### Fashion and Water: Fashion Revolution Japan’s new publication on clothing, water, and what the\n### industry can do to make a difference\n\n### TENCEL™ creative circle: Revealing our latest collaboration with Marc O'Polo\n\n### Performance, engineered from nature.\n\n### A vision for performance apparel’s future: The Mills Fabrica unveils new exhibition “Performance\n### Without Toxicity” in London\n\n### The 1 Granary TENCEL™ Club: Simon Giuliani, Candiani\n\n### In a simple world, what three policies or actions would you implement to achieve a more\n### sustainable way of life?\n\nTENCEL™ Lab\n\nOur innovation partnerships fuel the discovery of groundbreaking, industry leading technology.\n\n[Man in a blue shirt with arms crossed, standing in a laboratory setting with blurred equipment in\nthe background.]\nLAB\n\nA brighter future: What’s ahead for TENCEL™\n\n[Read more][37]\nLAB\n\nSmart Partnership: Lenzing and OceanSafe partner to launch next-gen yarn that blends wood-based\nTENCEL™ Lyocell - A100 fibers with biodegradable naNea co-polyester\n\n[Read more][38]\nLAB\n\nPushing the boundaries for a more circular future for textiles\n\n[Read more][39]\n\n##### TENCEL™ in Our Lives\n\n[\n[Ready to Wear]\n\n### Ready to Wear\n\n][40]\n[\n[Intimate]\n\n### Intimate\n\n][41]\n[\n[Footwear]\n\n### Footwear\n\n][42]\n[\n[Activewear]\n\n### Activewear\n\n][43]\n[\n[Denim]\n\n### Denim\n\n][44]\n[\n[Home]\n\n### Home\n\n][45]\n[ARROWS_LEFT_ICON]\n[ARROWS_RIGHT_ICON]\n[See all][46]\n[Explore more][47]\n“Every decision we make reflects the kind of world we want to live in.”\n[Nature][48]\n[Future][49]\n[Us][50]\n[Our Fibers][51]\n[What is TENCEL™][52]\n[Fiber Benefits][53]\n[TENCEL™ in our Lives][54]\n[Substantiation][55]\n\n### Connect With Us\n\n[Nature][56]\n[Future][57]\n[Us][58]\n[Our Fibers][59]\n[What is TENCEL™][60]\n[Fiber Benefits][61]\n[TENCEL™ in our Lives][62]\n[Substantiation][63]\n\n\nLenzing Aktiengesellschaft Werkstraße 2, 4860 Lenzing, Austria\n\nT: [+43 7672 7010][64]\nF: +43 7672 7013880\nE: [[email protected]][65]\n\nCopyright 2025 Lenzing AG\n[Lenzing][66]\n[Data Policy][67]\n[Terms of Use][68]\n[GTC][69]\n[Contact][70]\n[Legal Notice][71]\n[TENCEL™ for Business][72]\nCopyright 2025 Lenzing AG\n[TENCEL™ for Business][73]\nThis website uses cookies!\n\nClick on “Allow all cookies” to accept our analysis cookies or click on “Reject” to permit only the\ncookies\n\nwhich are absolute necessary to operate the website.\n\nYou can find detailed information [here][74]\n\nAllow all cookiesReject\n"
