          "text": "×\n\n###### Log In\n\nSign Up\n\n## Log In\n\nLog in to save your progress and obtain a certificate in Alison’s free Diploma in Web\n\nUsername:\nPassword:\n\n###### or\n\n###### Sign up with your Social Account\n\nKeep me logged in\nLog in\nDont have an Tutor account? Sign Up\n×\nLog in\n\n###### Sign Up\n\n## Sign up\n\nSign up to save your progress and obtain a certificate in Alison’s free Diploma in Web\n\nYour Name:\nEmail:\nPassword:\nPassword:\n\n###### or\n\n###### Sign up with your Social Account\n\nI agree to the Terms and Conditions Yes, I want to get the most out of Tutor by receiving tips,\nupdates and exclusive offers.\nSign In\nAlready have an Alison account? Log In\n[VAeng][1]\n* [Blog][2]\n* [Service][3]\n* [Category][4]\n  * [engineering-news][5]\n  * [equip][6]\n  * [professionals][7]\n  * [contractors][8]\n  * [consultants][9]\n  * [guestarticle][10]\n  * [feature][11]\n  * [move][12]\n  * [news][13]\n  * [bids-rfp-rfq][14]\n  * [vaengmail][15]\n  * [representatives][16]\n  * [print][17]\n  * [interactive][18]\n  * [advertise][19]\n  * [jobs][20]\n  * [societies][21]\n  * [schools][22]\n  * [equipment_suppliers][23]\n  * [professional-services][24]\n  * [engineering-contractors][25]\n  * [manufacturers-reps][26]\n  * [engineering-consultants][27]\nSign Up Login\nCategories\n[engineering-news][28]\n[equip][29]\n[professionals][30]\n[contractors][31] [consultants][32]\n[guestarticle][33]\n[feature][34]\n[move][35] [news][36]\n[bids-rfp-rfq][37]\n[vaengmail][38]\n[representatives][39] [print][40]\n[interactive][41]\n[advertise][42]\n[jobs][43] [societies][44]\n[schools][45]\n[equipment_suppliers][46]\n[professional-services][47] [engineering-contractors][48]\n[manufacturers-reps][49]\n[engineering-consultants][50]\n\n# BDM Construction Inc.\n1. [Home][51]\n2. [Bristol][52]\n3. [Roof Repair][53]\n4. BDM Construction Inc.\n\n## BDM Construction Inc.\n\n[BDM Construction Inc.]\n\nBDM Construction Inc.\n\n304 Garfield Dr, Kingsport, TN 37664\n\n──────────┬────────────────────────────────────────\nThursday  │* 8AM–5PM                               \n          │Holiday hours Hours might differ        \n──────────┼────────────────────────────────────────\nFriday    │* 8AM–5PM                               \n          │Holiday hours Hours might differ        \n──────────┼────────────────────────────────────────\nSaturday  │* Closed                                \n          │Holiday hours Hours might differ        \n──────────┼────────────────────────────────────────\nSunday    │* Closed                                \n          │Holiday hours Hours might differ        \n──────────┼────────────────────────────────────────\nMonday    │* 8AM–5PM                               \n          │Holiday hours Hours might differ        \n──────────┼────────────────────────────────────────\nTuesday   │* 8AM–5PM                               \n          │Holiday hours Hours might differ        \n──────────┼────────────────────────────────────────\nWednesday │* 8AM–5PM                               \n          │Holiday hours Hours might differ        \n──────────┴────────────────────────────────────────\n\n\n\n4.9 (130)\n\n##### Description:\n\n-\n\n### Reviews\n\n[ Write review][54]\n\n[Chance Garza][55] Sept. 2, 2022, 6:15 a.m.\n\nAverage rating:\n5.0 / 5.0\n\nThis is a busy roofing season. With that in mind, we contacted them, signed a contract and had our\nnew roof installed in 6 weeks time. This was amazing! We even had calls to let us know we was not\nforgotten. The day after the material arrived the crew showed up. The crew was amazing. In 90 degree\nheat, they worked on ...through it. I would recommend this company to anyone. From the beginning of\nthis project to the end was people doing the job they was supposed to do. They did everything they\nsaid they would. We was going to chose from 5 quotes. However, one didn't even call back until we\nsigned a contract. The other one did not have a good review. Their price was better than all of\nthem. Our roof is gorgeous. I'm so glad we chose BDM. Thanks to each one that called, quoted,\ninstalled and cleaned up. You are the BEST!!! More text\n\n[Akiko Reyes][56] Sept. 2, 2022, 6:15 a.m.\n\nAverage rating:\n5.0 / 5.0\n\nI called around looking for a company that could repair my leaking skylight and BDM was literally\nthe first one that could. Amanda took my call and was so friendly and was able to send Dusty out\nwithin a few days. He was very courteous and professional. He assessed my skylight and determined\nthere was a small leak c...ausing interior leaking into my condo. He suggested the repairs needed.\nHe came back a second time and met with my insurance adjuster to further review with him the\nsituation secure the funds needed for the repairs. He really went above and beyond. Jared then\nhandled scheduling the skylight repair work and interior painting and it was done in a timely and\nprofessional manner. The professionalism and courteousness I experienced from BDM was amazing. I\nwould highly recommend BDM to anyone. More text\n\n[Jerrod Mcgee][57] Sept. 2, 2022, 6:15 a.m.\n\nAverage rating:\n5.0 / 5.0\n\nI cannot say kind enough things about the people I had the pleasure of encountering during this\nprocess. First off my advice to you is to be patient because they stay booked for a reason but will\ncommunicate very well with you about everything. Michael was kind and knowledgeable when he arrived\nexactly on time for my e...stimate. The woman in the office is awesome and so helpful and has a\nsuper memory (and I can’t remember her name because I do not share her superpower.) Jared really\ndeserves a medal because he was the one that dealt with me and my ridiculous requests the most. I\nwas impressed with the crew that showed up to work on my roof as they were so speedy! They protected\nall my bushes and plants near the house (to my pleasant surprise) and made sure not to leave any\nmess at all. Everyone was hard at work so I communicated with them very little but when I did they\nwere friendly and knowledgeable. Their clear dedication and attention to detail is obvious in each\naspect of this process. My entire roof (~1k square feet) was removed, damaged areas repaired, and a\nnew roof installed in a single day. I got up there a little later to check everything out and it is\nPERFECT. Long story short—give them a call because they will take care of you!! More text\n\n[Boyce Mcmahon][58] Sept. 2, 2022, 6:15 a.m.\n\nAverage rating:\n5.0 / 5.0\n\nWonderful experience, highly recommend! We worked with Jared Malone, he helped us every step of the\nway with our complete roof replacement from our first meeting to when the project was finished and\nhe came back out to ensure everything was just right (which it was!). We have a custom home which\nmade for a potentially... tricky situation due to the original builder's design, initially we were\nnot sure what material we needed or if we needed to change the pitch with additional construction\nwork. After we met with Jared, he educated us and simplified our options which helped us to feel\nconfident, which brought peace of mind because this was a significant investment and we wanted to be\nsure we wouldn't have trouble later on with the complexities we had to work out. He gave us the pros\nand cons to all the options but left the final decisions up to us in a no-pressure fashion. This was\nrefreshing because we had previously met with another constructor prior to finding BDM, the other\ncompany did not have our confidence because they did not offer choices, they told us one way it had\nto be, they had higher prices and poor communication. BDM was great, everyone was responsive in\ncommunicating, their prices beat the other company's quote and most importantly have our trust and a\ncustomer for life. We've really liked all the guys on the work crew. They've all been very friendly,\npolite and very respectful. They have a great team, we appreciate all of them, they worked hard and\nefficiantly. We didn't worry about leaving to go to work while they were there. They cleaned up all\nthe scrap material and left everything so nice, they went around with special tools to ensure no\nnails were left behind after the drop cloths were taken away. It feels good having people you trust\nat your home. More text\n\n## Posts navigation\n\n[ prev Previous page][59] [Page 1][60] Page 2\n\n#### Write review\n\nLeave feedback as: Send\n\n### You may be interested\n\n[[Dixie Builders]\n\nDixie Builders\n\n][61]\n[[Gibson's Roofing]\n\nGibson's Roofing\n\n][62]\n[[Eddie Davidson Plumbing]\n\nEddie Davidson Plumbing\n\n][63]\n[[Double R Construction Co]\n\nDouble R Construction Co\n\n][64]\n[[Kingsport Roofing Pros]\n\nKingsport Roofing Pros\n\n][65]\n[[Leonard Roofing]\n\nLeonard Roofing\n\n][66]\n[[Baker Roofing Company]\n\nBaker Roofing Company\n\n][67]\n[[Tri-Cities Roofing]\n\nTri-Cities Roofing\n\n][68]\nInformation Partnerships:\n\n### Follow us\n\n### Contacts\n\nThe Farm SoHo NYC - Coworking Office Space 447 Broadway 2nd floor, New York, NY 10013, US\n\n+1 917-722-5027\n\n© 2023 vaeng.com\n\n[1]: /\n[2]: /articles/\n[3]: /service/\n[4]: \n[5]: /engineering-news/\n[6]: /equips/\n[7]: /professionals/\n[8]: /contractors/\n[9]: /consultants/\n[10]: /guestarticle/\n[11]: /feature/\n[12]: /move/\n[13]: /news/\n[14]: /bids-rfp-rfq/\n[15]: /vaengmail/\n[16]: /representatives/\n[17]: /print/\n[18]: /interactive/\n[19]: /advertise/\n[20]: /jobs/\n[21]: /societies/\n[22]: /schools/\n[23]: /equipmentsuppliers/\n[24]: /professional-services/\n[25]: /engineering-contractors/\n[26]: /manufacturers-reps/\n[27]: /engineering-consultants/\n[28]: /engineering-news/\n[29]: /equips/\n[30]: /professionals/\n[31]: /contractors/\n[32]: /consultants/\n[33]: /guestarticle/\n[34]: /feature/\n[35]: /move/\n[36]: /news/\n[37]: /bids-rfp-rfq/\n[38]: /vaengmail/\n[39]: /representatives/\n[40]: /print/\n[41]: /interactive/\n[42]: /advertis